hadiths[249]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","It is narrated from Abu Amr Shaibani who says: The owner of this house narrated a hadith to us, and with his hand he pointed towards the house of Sayyiduna Abdullah (bin Mas'ud) (may Allah be pleased with him), that he said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), ""Which deed is most beloved to Allah the Exalted?"" He said: ""To perform the prayer at its earliest time."" I said: ""Then which?"" He said: ""Then to treat parents with kindness."" I said: ""Then which?"" He said: ""Then striving in the way of Allah."" (Ibn Mas'ud) said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told me these deeds, and if I had asked for more, he would have told me more."
"2","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that he said: The pleasure of the Lord is in the pleasure of the father, and the displeasure of the Lord is in the displeasure of the father."
"3","It is narrated from Bahz bin Hakim, from his father, and he from his grandfather: I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! With whom should I behave kindly?"" He said, ""With your mother."" I asked, ""Then with whom should I behave kindly?"" He said, ""With your mother."" I asked, ""Then with whom should I behave kindly?"" He said, ""With your mother."" I asked, ""Then with whom should I behave kindly?"" He said, ""With your father, then those who are closest to you, then those who are next closest."""
"4","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that a man came to him and said: I proposed marriage to a woman, but she refused to marry me. Another man proposed to her, and she preferred to marry him. I was overcome with jealousy and killed that woman. Is there any repentance for me? He asked: Is your mother alive? The man replied: No. He said: Repent to Allah and seek closeness to Him as much as you are able. Ata bin Yasar says: I went and asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them): Why did you ask him whether his mother was alive? He replied: I do not know of any deed that brings one closer to Allah than being good to one’s mother."
"5","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: ""With whom should I behave kindly?"" He replied: ""With your mother."" He was asked: ""Then with whom?"" He replied: ""With your mother."" He was asked: ""Then with whom?"" He replied: ""With your mother."" He was asked: ""Then with whom?"" (Then, on the fourth time, he turned and) replied: ""With your father."""
"6","It is narrated from Taysalah bin Miyaas, he says: I was with Najdah bin Aamir, a follower of the Khawarij (this is a group of Khawarij). I committed such sins which I considered to be major sins, so I mentioned this to Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them). He asked: Which sins are those? I said: Such and such. He said: These are not major sins. The major sins are nine: associating partners with Allah, killing a soul, fleeing from battle, accusing a chaste woman of adultery, consuming usury, consuming the wealth of an orphan, committing disbelief (irreligion) in the mosque, the person who mocks (the religion), and making the parents weep due to disobedience (of the son). Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) said to me: Do you fear Hell and wish to enter Paradise? I said: Yes, by Allah. He asked: Are your parents alive? I said: My mother is with me. He said: By Allah! If you speak gently to her and feed her, you will enter Paradise as long as you avoid major sins."
"7","It is narrated from Urwah, he said: «‏ وَاخْفِضْ لَهُمَا جَنَاحَ الذُّلِّ مِنَ الرَّحْمَةِ ‏» ""Lower the wings of humility out of mercy before them."" And he said: Do not refuse anything that your parents like."
"8","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he narrated from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: ""No child can repay his father except that if he finds him as a slave, he should buy him and set him free."""
"9","It is narrated from Abu Burdah that he was present with Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) and a Yemeni man was performing Tawaf of the Ka'bah. He had his mother lifted on his back and was saying: ""I am her obedient camel; if her mounts are frightened, I will not be frightened."" Then that man said: ""O Ibn Umar! Do you think I have repaid my mother?"" He said: ""No, not even for a single sigh of hers."" Then Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) performed Tawaf, came to the Maqam Ibrahim, prayed two rak'ahs, and then said: ""O son of Abu Musa! Each two rak'ahs erase the sins that were committed before."""
"10","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and pledged allegiance to him for migration, and he had left his parents in a state that they were crying. The Prophet said: ""Go back to them, and make them laugh as you made them cry."""
"11","Abu Murrah, the freed slave of Umm Hani, narrated (she was the daughter of Abu Talib), that she told him that she went riding with Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) to his land which was in a place called Al-Aqiq. When he entered his land, he called out loudly: O my mother! « عَلَيْكِ السَّلاَمُ وَرَحْمَةُ اللهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهُ » She said: « وَعَلَيْكَ السَّلاَمُ وَرَحْمَةُ اللهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهُ » He said: « رَحِمَكِ اللَّهُ رَبَّيْتِنِي صَغِيرًا » So she said: « يَا بُنَيَّ ، وَأَنْتَ فَجَزَاكَ اللَّهُ خَيْرًا وَرَضِيَ عَنْكَ كَمَا بَرَرْتَنِي كَبِيرًا » Musa says that the name of Abu Hurairah was Abdullah bin Amr."
"12","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said three times: ""Shall I not inform you of the greatest of the major sins?"" The companions said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Certainly."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Associating partners with Allah and disobedience to parents."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) was reclining, then he sat up and said: ""Listen, and false speech."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) kept repeating it until I said: I wished he would be silent."
"13","It is narrated from Abu Tufail that Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked, ""Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) tell you anything that he did not tell anyone else among the people?"" Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not tell us anything that he did not tell others, except what is in the sheath of my sword."" Then he took out a scroll (from the sheath of the sword), and it was written in it: ""May Allah curse the one who sacrifices in the name of other than Allah, may Allah curse the one who steals the boundary marker of the land, may Allah curse the one who curses his parents, may Allah curse the one who gives shelter to an innovator."""
"14","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Darda’ (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advised me regarding nine things. They are: Even if you are cut into pieces or burned, do not associate anything with Allah; never deliberately abandon the obligatory prayer, for whoever deliberately abandons it, the protection (of Allah and His Messenger) is lifted from him; never drink alcohol, for it is the key to every evil; obey your parents, even if they command you to give up your worldly possessions (meaning, hand over all your belongings to them), then do so for their sake; do not dispute with the rulers, even if you think you are entitled (i.e., you alone are upon the truth); never flee from the battlefield, even if you are killed and your companions flee; spend on your family from your wealth; do not withhold your stick from your family (meaning, maintain the disciplinary rod for their upbringing); and keep warning them about Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."
"15","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man came to the service of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, intending to go for jihad. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, asked: ""Are your parents alive?"" He replied: Yes. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Then go and strive in their service (serve them, that is your jihad)."""
"16","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “May his nose be rubbed in dust, may his nose be rubbed in dust, may his nose be rubbed in dust.” The Companions asked: O Messenger of Allah! Whose? He said: “The one who finds his parents, both of them, or one of them, in old age and then enters Hell.”"
"17","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding the saying of Allah the Exalted: «‏ إِمَّا يَبْلُغَنَّ عِنْدَكَ الْكِبَرَ أَحَدُهُمَا أَوْ كِلاَهُمَا فَلاَ تَقُلْ لَهُمَا أُفٍّ » ""If one or both of them reach old age with you, do not say to them 'uff'..."" up to His saying: « كَمَا رَبَّيَانِي صَغِيرًا ‏» ""...as they brought me up when I was small."" This was abrogated by the verse of Surah Bara’ah: « مَا كَانَ لِلنَّبِيِّ وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا أَنْ يَسْتَغْفِرُوا لِلْمُشْرِكِينَ وَلَوْ كَانُوا أُولِي قُرْبَى مِنْ بَعْدِ مَا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُمْ أَنَّهُمْ أَصْحَابُ الْجَحِيمِ » ""It is not for the Prophet and those who believe to ask forgiveness for the polytheists, even if they are close relatives, after it has become clear to them that they are the companions of the Fire."""
"18","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: Four verses of the Qur’an were revealed about me. My mother had sworn an oath that she would neither eat nor drink until I left the company of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). At that time, Allah the Exalted revealed this verse: « وَإِنْ جَاهَدَاكَ عَلَى أَنْ تُشْرِكَ بِي مَا لَيْسَ لَكَ بِهِ عِلْمٌ فَلاَ تُطعهُمَا وَصَاحِبْهُمَا فِي الدُّنْيَا مَعْرُوفًا » “And if they both strive to make you associate with Me that of which you have no knowledge, then do not obey them, but accompany them in this world with kindness.” The second verse: I took a sword that I liked. I said: O Messenger of Allah! Grant it to me as a gift. Upon this, the following verse was revealed: «‏ يَسْأَلُونَكَ عَنِ الأَنْفَالِ » “They ask you about the spoils of war.” And the third verse: I fell ill. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me. I said: O Messenger of Allah! I want to distribute my wealth among the poor and needy. May I bequeath half of my wealth? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “No.” I said: What about a third? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent, but after him, bequeathing a third became permissible. And the fourth verse: I drank wine with some of the Ansar, and one of them struck my nose with a camel’s jawbone. I presented myself before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Allah the Exalted revealed the verse regarding the prohibition of wine."
"19","It is narrated from Sayyida Asma bint Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: In the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), my mother came to me, inclined towards Islam. I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Should I maintain ties of kinship with her? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Yes."" Ibn Uyaynah says that Allah the Exalted then revealed this verse: «‏ لاَ يَنْهَاكُمُ اللَّهُ عَنِ الَّذِينَ لَمْ يُقَاتِلُوكُمْ فِي الدِّينِ » ""Allah does not forbid you from those who have not fought you because of religion, to deal kindly and justly with them."""
"20","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) saw a silk cloak being sold and said: O Messenger of Allah! Buy this and wear it on Fridays or when a delegation comes to you. He (the Prophet ﷺ) said: ""Such clothing is worn by those who have no share (in the Hereafter)."" Then some cloaks of that kind were brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he sent one cloak to Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). So Umar said: How can I wear it when you have already said what you had to say about it? He (the Prophet ﷺ) said: ""I did not give it to you so that you wear it yourself, but so that you may sell it and benefit from it, or dress your women with it."" So Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) sent that cloak to his brother in Makkah, and he had not yet accepted Islam."
"21","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Among the major sins is that a person abuses his parents."" The Companions asked in astonishment: How can anyone abuse his parents? He replied: ""He abuses another man, so that man (in response) abuses his father and his mother."""
"22","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: Among the major sins is that a person becomes the cause of abuse for his own father."
"23","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no sin more deserving that its doer be hastily punished (in this world), along with what is stored for him (in the Hereafter), than oppression and severing ties of kinship."""
"24","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There are three types of supplications that are accepted, about whose acceptance there is no doubt: the supplication of the oppressed, the supplication of the traveler, and the supplication of a father against his son."""
"25","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""No child has spoken in the cradle except ‘Isa ibn Maryam (peace be upon him) and the child of Jurayj."" The people asked: O Prophet of Allah! Who is the child of Jurayj? He said: ""Jurayj was a devout worshipper and a monk, and he was in his place of worship. A cowherd used to stay at night beneath his place of worship. A woman from among the people of that village used to come and go to that cowherd. One day, Jurayj’s mother came to him and said: O Jurayj! And he was praying. Jurayj thought to himself while he was praying: My mother is calling me and I am praying. He thought to himself to give preference to his prayer. Then she called out to him again. He thought: My mother is calling me and I am praying, so he decided to give preference to his prayer. Then for the third time she called out. Again he thought: My mother is calling me and I am praying. He decided to give preference to his prayer. When Jurayj did not answer his mother, she said: O Jurayj! May Allah not let you die until you have faced immoral women. Then she went away. That (village) woman was brought to the king, and she had given birth to a child. The king asked: Whose boy is this? She said: Jurayj’s. The king said: The one who stays in the place of worship? She said: Yes. The king ordered: Demolish Jurayj’s place of worship and bring him to me. The people attacked his place of worship with axes until it fell down. They tied his hands to his neck with ropes. Then he was brought. He was made to pass by the immoral women, and when he saw them, he smiled, and they were looking at him among the people. The king said (to Jurayj): (Do you know) what this woman is saying? He said: What is she saying? He said: She is saying that this child is from you. He said to the woman: Are you saying this? She said: Yes. Jurayj said: Where is the little child? They said: He is in her lap. So he turned towards him and asked the child: Who is your father? The child said: The cowherd. The king said: Shall I have your place of worship built of gold? Jurayj said: No. He said: Of silver? He said: No. He said: What shall we build it of? He said: Build it as it was. The king said: What was the reason that you smiled? Jurayj said: It was a matter that I knew. My mother’s supplication against me had reached me. Then he narrated the whole story to the people."""
"26","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) who says: Whoever among the Christians and Jews hears about me, will love me. Whenever I tried to persuade my mother to accept Islam, she would refuse. I asked her (once again to become Muslim), but she refused. So I went to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Pray to Allah for my mother. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed. After that, I went to my mother. She had closed the door. She said: O Abu Hurairah! I have become Muslim. I informed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Pray for me and my mother. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: « اللَّهُمَّ ، عَبْدُكَ أَبُو هُرَيْرَةَ وَأُمُّهُ ، أَحِبَّهُمَا إِلَى النَّاسِ » ""O Allah! Your servant Abu Hurairah and his mother—make both of them beloved in the eyes of the people."""
"27","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The ranks of the deceased are elevated even after his death. So he asks: O my Lord! Which deed is it because of which my ranks have been elevated? It is said: Your son has sought forgiveness for you."
"28","It is narrated from Muhammad bin Sirin that he said: One night we were with Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), so he said: « اللَّهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لأَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ ، وَلِأُمِّي ، وَلِمَنِ اسْتَغْفَرَ لَهُمَا » ""O Allah! Forgive me and my mother, and forgive all those who seek forgiveness for both of us."" Muhammad said to me: We will continue to seek forgiveness for both of them so that we may be included in the supplication of Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"29","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When a person dies, his deeds come to an end except for three: ongoing charity, knowledge from which benefit is derived, or a righteous child who prays for him."""
"30","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that a man said: O Messenger of Allah! My mother has passed away and she did not make any will. If I give charity on her behalf, will it benefit her? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Yes."""
"31","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""The greatest act of goodness is that a person treats well the friends of his father."""
"32","It is narrated from Urwah or someone else that Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) saw two men, so he asked one of them: ""What is your relation to him?"" He replied: ""He is my father."" So Abu Hurairah said: ""Do not call him by his name, do not walk ahead of him, and do not sit before him."""
"33","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that he said: But as for Abu Hafs Umar, this is his decision. (He mentioned his father's kunyah.) (Among the Arabs, calling someone by their kunyah is considered a great sign of respect.)"
"34","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that when this verse was revealed «‏ وَأَنْذِرْ عَشِيرَتَكَ الأَقْرَبِينَ » ""And warn your nearest kindred,"" the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up and called out: ""O Banu Ka'b bin Lu'ayy! Save yourselves from the Fire. O Banu 'Abd Manaf! Save yourselves from the Fire. O Banu Hashim! Save yourselves from the Fire. O Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib! Save yourselves from the Fire. O Fatimah bint Muhammad! Save yourself from the Fire. I have no power to save you from Allah; however, there is a relationship and connection between us, and I will continue to fulfill its rights."""
"35","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) that during a journey of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a Bedouin came before him and said, ""Tell me of an action that will bring me near to Paradise and keep me far from Hell."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Worship Allah, do not associate anything with Him, establish prayer, give zakat, and maintain the ties of kinship."""
"36","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, created the creation and finished with it, the bond of kinship stood up."" Allah said: ""What is the matter?"" It said: ""This is the place of one who seeks refuge with You from being cut off."" Allah said: ""Are you not pleased that I will keep ties with the one who keeps ties with you, and I will cut off the one who cuts you off?"" The bond of kinship said: ""Yes, O my Lord! I am pleased."" He said: ""This is for you."" Then Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: If you wish, recite this verse: «‏ فَهَلْ عَسَيْتُمْ إِنْ تَوَلَّيْتُمْ أَنْ تُفْسِدُوا فِي الأَرْضِ وَتُقَطِّعُوا أَرْحَامَكُمْ » ""Then, would you perhaps, if you turned away, cause corruption on earth and sever your ties of kinship?"""
"37","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: A man came to the service of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah! I have some relatives. I maintain ties with them, but they sever relations with me. I treat them well, but they treat me badly. They behave ignorantly (quarrel) with me, and I deal with them with patience and forbearance. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""If it is as you say, then it is as if you are putting hot ashes into their mouths. And as long as you remain in this state, a helper from Allah against them will always be with you."""
"38","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says: ""I am the Most Merciful (Rahman) and I have created the womb (rahm), and I have derived its name from My Name. Whoever joins it, I will join him, and whoever severs it, I will sever him."""
"39","It is narrated from Abu Anbas, he states that I went to Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) at ""Wahat"", that is, the land he had in Taif. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bent his finger before us and said: ""Kinship is a branch that has come from the Most Merciful. Whoever maintains it, (Allah) will maintain him, and whoever breaks it, He will break him. On the Day of Resurrection, it will have a tongue that will speak rapidly."""
"40","Narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The womb (rahm) is derived from the name of Allah. Whoever maintains its ties, Allah will maintain ties with him, and whoever severs it, Allah will sever ties with him."""
"41","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever wishes that his provision be expanded for him and his life be prolonged for him, he should maintain the ties of kinship."""
"42","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever wishes that his provision be expanded for him and his life be prolonged, he should maintain the ties of kinship."
"43","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he said: Whoever fears his Lord and maintains the ties of kinship, his life is lengthened (his death is delayed), his wealth is increased, and the members of his household love him."
"44","It is narrated from Miqdam bin Ma'dikarib that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: Indeed, Allah enjoins you to treat your mothers well, then He enjoins you to treat your mothers well, then your fathers, then He enjoins you to treat the closest relative after them well, then the next closest after him."
"45","It is narrated from Jubair bin Mut'im that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say: ""The one who severs the ties of kinship will not enter Paradise."""
"46","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""The womb is a root that has sprung from the Most Merciful, and it says: O my Lord! I have been wronged. O my Lord! I have been severed (i.e., the right of my relationship has not been fulfilled). O my Lord! I have been oppressed, I have been oppressed, « يَا رَبِّ » , « يَا رَبِّ » . (Allah Almighty) answers it: Are you not pleased that I will cut off the one who severs you, and I will join the one who joins you?"""
"47","Saeed bin Sam'an narrates, he says: I heard from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he used to seek refuge from the rule of boys and fools."
"48","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him). He said that the Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no sin more deserving that Allah should hasten its punishment in this world, along with what He has stored for it in the Hereafter, than severing ties of kinship and committing injustice."""
"49","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The one who maintains ties of kinship is not the one who does so in return for receiving it, but the one who truly maintains ties of kinship is the one who, when his ties are severed, he still maintains them."""
"50","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Bara’ (may Allah be pleased with him) that a Bedouin came and said: O Messenger of Allah! Teach me a deed that will admit me into Paradise. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “If only you had kept your question brief, but you have made it lengthy. Free a slave and set a neck free.” He said: Are these two not the same? He replied: “No, freeing a slave means that you completely free a slave, and setting a neck free means that you help in freeing a slave. And give as a gift an animal that gives much milk, and spend on your relatives. If you do not have the ability to do this, then enjoin good and forbid evil, and if you do not have the ability to do even this, then restrain your tongue except for speaking good.”"
"51","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Hakim bin Hizam (may Allah be pleased with him) that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What is your opinion about those acts of worship that I used to do in the days of ignorance, such as maintaining ties of kinship, freeing slaves, and giving charity? Will I also receive reward for them? Hakim says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You have accepted Islam along with all the good deeds you did before (in the days of ignorance)."" (That is, you will also receive their reward.)"
"52","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that once Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) saw a cloak in which some silk was mixed, so he said: ""O Messenger of Allah! If you buy this cloak and wear it on Fridays or when delegations come to you."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Umar! Only those people wear it who have no share (in the Hereafter)."" After that, some of those cloaks were given to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent one of those cloaks to Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). So Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! You have sent this to me, even though I have heard from you about it."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I did not give it to you so that you wear it, but I gave it to you so that you may sell it, or make someone else wear it, or give it to someone."" So Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) gave it to his half-brother, who was a polytheist."
"53","53/72 From Jubayr ibn Mut'im, who heard Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, say on the pulpit: ""Learn your genealogies, then maintain your ties of kinship. By Allah, there may be something between a man and his brother, but if he knew what was between them of the bond of the womb, that would restrain him from violating it."""
"54","54/73 - From Ibn Abbas; he said: ""Preserve your lineages, and you will maintain your ties of kinship; for there is no distance with kinship when it is maintained, even if it is far, and there is no closeness with it when it is severed, even if it is near. Every kinship will come on the Day of Resurrection before its owner, testifying for him if he maintained it, and against him if he severed it."""
"55","55/75 From Rifa‘ah ibn Rafi‘; that the Prophet, peace be upon him, said to ‘Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: ""Gather your people for me."" So he gathered them, and when they arrived at the door of the Prophet, peace be upon him, ‘Umar entered upon him and said: I have gathered my people for you. The Ansar heard of this and said: Revelation has descended upon Quraysh, so those who wished to listen and observe what would be said to them came. The Prophet, peace be upon him, came out and stood among them and said: ""Is there anyone among you who is not of you?"" They said: Yes, among us is our ally, the son of our sister, and our freedmen. The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""Our ally is one of us, the son of our sister is one of us, and our freedmen are one of us. And you hear: Indeed, my friends among you are the righteous; if you are those, then so be it, otherwise beware lest people come on the Day of Resurrection with deeds, and you come with burdens, and He will turn away from you."" Then he called out and said: ""O people! – and he raised his hands and placed them on the heads of Quraysh – O people! Quraysh are people of trustworthiness; whoever seeks to harm them – (Zuhair said: I think he said: with misfortunes) – Allah will throw him down on his nose."" He said this three times."
"56","56/76 From Uqbah ibn Amir who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say: ""Whoever has three daughters, and is patient with them, and clothes them from his wealth, they will be a shield for him from the Fire."""
"57","57/77 From Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace be upon him, who said: ""No Muslim who is entrusted with two daughters and treats them kindly, but they will admit him to Paradise."""
"58","58/78 From Jabir ibn Abdullah, he narrated to them, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever has three daughters, shelters them, provides for them, and shows mercy to them, Paradise is certainly guaranteed for him."" A man from among the people said: And two, O Messenger of Allah? He said: ""And two."""
"59","59/97 From Abu Sa'id al-Khudri; that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""No one has three daughters, or three sisters, and treats them well, except that he will enter Paradise."""
"60","60/82 From al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib; he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, say: ""Whatever you feed yourself is charity for you, and whatever you feed your child is charity for you, and whatever you feed your wife is charity for you, and whatever you feed your servant is charity for you."""
"61","61/84 From Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said one day: ""By Allah, there is no man on the face of the earth more beloved to me than Umar."" Then when he left and came back, he said: ""How did I swear, O little daughter?"" So I told him. He said: ""You are dearer to me, and the child is more attached.""(2)"
"62","62/58 From Ibn Abi Nu'm, he said: I was present with Ibn Umar when a man asked him about the blood of a mosquito. He said: ""Where are you from?"" He replied: ""From the people of Iraq."" He said: ""Look at this one, he asks me about the blood of a mosquito, while they have killed the son of the Prophet, peace be upon him. I heard the Prophet, peace be upon him, say: 'They are my two sweet basils from this world.'"""
"63","63/68 From Al-Bara’ who said: I saw the Prophet, peace be upon him, and Al-Hasan—blessings of Allah be upon him—was on his shoulder, and he was saying: ""O Allah! I love him, so love him."""
"64","It is narrated from Jubair bin Nufair that he said: One day we were sitting with Miqdad bin Aswad. Then a man passed by him and said: How fortunate and blessed are those two eyes that saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). By Allah, our hearts desire that we too had seen what you saw and participated in those (battles) in which you participated. Upon this, Sayyiduna Miqdad (may Allah be pleased with him) became angry. So I was surprised that he had said a good thing (why is he getting angry). After that, Miqdad (may Allah be pleased with him) turned towards him and said: Why does a man wish for things from which Allah has kept him absent? He does not know what his role would have been if he had been there? By Allah, there were also people who saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) whom Allah threw face down into Hell. Because they did not obey the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), nor did they affirm him. Do you not praise Allah, the Exalted, for the fact that when He created you in this world, you did not know anyone except your Lord? And you affirm the Shariah that your Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) brought. (It is good) you have been saved from the trials through which the Companions passed. By Allah, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was sent in very difficult circumstances, in the time of ignorance and in the period of interruption of prophethood. No prophet was sent in such difficult circumstances. In those days, in the eyes of those people, no religion was better than idolatry. So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) brought such speech which was the Furqan, which distinguished between truth and falsehood. And through it, he created a distinction between father and son (that one would be a disbeliever and the other a Muslim). So much so that if a man saw his father, his son, and his brother in a state of disbelief, and Allah had opened the lock of his own heart with the key of faith, and he knew that his father, brother, or son who was a disbeliever, if he died in that state, he would enter Hell, then his eyes would not be cooled, and he knew that his beloved had gone to Hell. And the coolness of the eyes is only from that which Allah, the Exalted, has said: «‏ وَالَّذِينَ يَقُولُونَ رَبَّنَا هَبْ لَنَا مِنْ أَزْوَاجِنَا وَذُرِّيَّاتِنَا قُرَّةَ أَعْيُنٍ » ""And those who say: Our Lord, grant us from our wives and our offspring the coolness of our eyes."" (Meaning that they act upon the Shariah, because the believer's eyes will only be cooled by his children and wife when they are worshippers of Allah.)"
"65","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: One day I came to serve the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and only I, my mother, and my maternal aunt Umm Haram were present. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and said to us: ""Shall I not lead you in prayer?"" And it was not the time for obligatory prayer (meaning he wanted to offer a voluntary prayer). So one of the people said: Where did you make Anas stand? It was said: Anas was made to stand on the right side, then he led us in prayer. Then he supplicated for every good of this world and the Hereafter for the people of the household. Then my mother said: O Messenger of Allah! This is your humble servant, please pray to Allah for him as well. So he prayed for every good for me. The last words of your (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplication were: «اللهم أكثر ماله وولده ، وبارك له» ""O Allah! Increase his wealth and children and bless him in them."" (This means that if the children are righteous, there is no better wealth than this, and one should pray for its blessing.)"
"66","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that a woman came to Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her). Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) gave her three dates. She gave one each to her two children and kept one for herself. Both children ate their dates and began to look at their mother. She split the third date into two pieces and gave one piece to each child. After that, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came, so Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) related this incident to him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is nothing surprising in this; Allah the Exalted has shown mercy to her because she showed mercy to her two children."""
"67","It is narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that a Bedouin came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: ""Do you people kiss children? By Allah, we do not kiss them."" Upon this, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If Allah has removed mercy from your heart, then what can I do?"""
"68","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissed Sayyiduna Hasan bin Ali (may Allah be pleased with them both). At that time, Aqra’ bin Habis Tamimi was sitting with the Prophet (peace be upon him). Aqra’ said: “I have ten sons and I have not kissed any of them.” Upon this, the Messenger (peace be upon him) looked towards him and said: “He who does not show mercy will not be shown mercy.”"
"69","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Nu’man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), who said that his father took him and presented him before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And (his father) said to the Messenger (peace be upon him), “O Messenger of Allah! I want to make you a witness that I have given Nu’man such and such things.” The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “Have you given this gift to all your children?” He replied: “No.” The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “Then make someone else a witness.” After that, the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “Do you not like that all your children should be equal in showing kindness to you?” He replied: “Why not.” The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “Then do not do this.” Abu Abdullah Bukhari (may Allah have mercy on him) says: The testimony of the Prophet (peace be upon him) will not be considered as permission."
"70","Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: “Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy.”"
"71","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jarir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him). He said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Allah does not have mercy on the one who does not have mercy on people."" In another chain of narration, the words are: ""Whoever does not have mercy on people, Allah does not have mercy on him."""
"72","It is narrated from Abu Uthman that Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) appointed a man as an official. The official said: I have so many sons, but I have not kissed any of them. So Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) thought, or Umar said: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, only shows mercy to those among His servants who are the best in their conduct towards others."
"73","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say: ""Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, made mercy into one hundred parts. He kept ninety-nine parts with Himself and sent down only one part to the earth. It is because of this one part that people show mercy to one another, to the extent that a mare lifts its hoof so that it does not harm its foal."""
"74","Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Gabriel (peace be upon him) continued to advise me regarding the neighbor so much that I thought he would make the neighbor an heir."""
"75","Sayyiduna Abu Shurayh Khuzai (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: “Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should treat his neighbor well, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent.”"
"76","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Miqdad bin Aswad (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked his companions about adultery. The people replied: It is forbidden; Allah the Exalted and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) have declared it forbidden. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “If a man commits adultery with ten women, it is a lesser sin than committing adultery with his neighbor’s wife.” And he asked them: “What is your opinion about theft?” They said: It is forbidden; Allah the Exalted and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) have forbidden it. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “For a person to steal from ten houses is a lesser sin than to steal from the house of his neighbor.”"
"77","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Jibreel kept advising me regarding the neighbor so much that I thought he would surely make the neighbor an heir."""
"78","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) that when one of his goats was slaughtered, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) kept saying to his servant: ""Have you sent a gift to our Jewish neighbor? Have you sent a gift to our Jewish neighbor?"" I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Jibreel kept advising me regarding the neighbor so much that I thought he would make him an heir."""
"79","It is narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! I have two neighbors, to which of them should I send a gift?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""To the one whose door is closer to you."""
"80","Hasan (al-Basri) narrates that he was asked about the neighbor, so he said: forty houses in front (of your house), forty houses behind, forty houses to the right, and forty houses to the left. (That is, even the fortieth house is considered a neighbor.)"
"81","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he said: There was a time, or he said: A period came upon us when a person did not consider anyone more deserving of his dirhams and dinars than his Muslim brother. Now the time has come that dirhams and dinars are more beloved to us than our Muslim brother. I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say that many neighbors will cling to their neighbors on the Day of Resurrection. The neighbor will say: O my Lord! This person had closed his door upon me and withheld his favor from me."
"82","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Masawwar who says: I heard from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that he was telling Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: I heard from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that a Muslim is not one who eats his fill while his neighbor is hungry."
"83","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (Ghifari) رضي الله عنه that he said: My beloved friend Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم advised me with three things: “Listen and obey, even if it is a slave with mutilated ears (even if such a slave is made a ruler whose hands and feet are cut off). When you cook broth, increase its quantity and look at the houses of your neighbors and give to them (do good to them through this broth). And perform the prayer at its earliest time, and after that, if you see that the Imam has already performed the prayer, then you have attained your prayer, and if the Imam is yet to lead the prayer, then pray with him again; this will be counted as a voluntary prayer.” And in another narration with these words: “O Abu Dharr! When you cook broth, increase its water and take care of your neighbors or distribute it among your neighbors.”"
"84","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""The best companion in the sight of Allah is the one who is best to his companion, and the best neighbor in the sight of Allah is the one who is best to his neighbor."""
"85","Nafi' bin 'Abd al-Harith narrates from the Prophet (ﷺ) that he said: ""Among the good fortunes of a Muslim are: a spacious house, a righteous neighbor, and a pleasant mount."""
"86","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said that among the supplications of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was this supplication, « اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي أَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنْ جَارِ السُّوءِ فِي دَارِ الْمُقَامِ » ""O Allah! I seek refuge with You from an evil neighbor in residence."" Because the neighbor in this world moves away."
"87","It is narrated from Abu Musa, he said that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The Hour will not be established until a man kills his neighbor, his brother, and his father."""
"88","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that it was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""O Messenger of Allah! Such-and-such woman stands in prayer at night, fasts during the day, performs good deeds, gives charity, but hurts her neighbors with her tongue."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There is no good in her; she is among the people of Hell."" The people said: ""Such-and-such woman performs only the obligatory prayers, gives pieces of cheese in charity, and does not harm anyone."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""She is among the people of Paradise."""
"89","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""That person will not enter Paradise whose neighbor is not safe from his evil."""
"90","Amr bin Mu'adh Al-Ashhali narrates from his grandmother that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to me: ""O believing women! Let not any woman among you consider insignificant the gift she gives to her neighbor, even if it is only a burnt hoof of a goat."""
"91","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Muslim women! O Muslim women! Let not any woman among you consider insignificant giving a gift to her neighbor, even if it is only a sheep's hoof."""
"92","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: A man submitted, ""O Messenger of Allah! I have a neighbor who causes me harm."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Go, take your belongings out of your house and put them on the road."" He went and took his belongings out and placed them on the road. People gathered around him and began to ask, ""What happened to you?"" He said, ""My neighbor causes me harm. When I mentioned this to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said, 'Go and take your belongings out and put them on the road.'"" So all the people began to say, ""O Allah! Curse him, O Allah! Humiliate him."" When this reached the neighbor, he came to him and said, ""Go back to your house. By Allah, I will never harm you again."""
"93","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Juhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man complained to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) about his neighbor. So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pick up your belongings and put them on the road; whoever passes by will curse him."" So whoever passed by would curse him. Then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: ""What kind of treatment am I facing from the people?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah's curse is greater than their curse."" (If you cannot bear the curse of the people, then Allah's curse is upon the one who harms his neighbor.) Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to the man who had complained: ""This is sufficient for you."""
"94","It is narrated from Abu Amir Hamsi, he said that Sayyiduna Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say: Whenever two people keep a break in relations with each other for more than three days, then one of them is ruined. And if both die while maintaining this break, then both are destroyed. And if a person oppresses his neighbor and overpowers him to the extent that he forces him to leave his house, then such a person is destroyed."
"95","Mujahid narrates that I was with Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) and his servant was skinning a goat. He said: O boy! When you finish this task, first give the meat to our Jewish neighbor. One of the people said: May Allah set you right. To a Jew? He said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say—he used to emphasize so much about the neighbor that we feared or thought that he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would make him an heir."
"96","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Who is the most honorable among the people? He replied: ""The most honorable in the sight of Allah is the one who is most God-fearing."" The people said: We did not ask about this. He said: ""The most honorable among the people (in one narration: the most honorable son of the most honorable, his son the most honorable): Yusuf, who is a Prophet of Allah, the son of a Prophet of Allah, the son of Allah's Khalil (who himself is a Prophet, the son of a Prophet of Allah, and the great-grandson of Allah's Khalil) (Yusuf son of Yaqub son of Ishaq son of Ibrahim)."" The people said: We are not asking about this either. He said: ""Are you asking about the tribes of the Arabs?"" The people said: Yes. He said: ""Those who were the best among you in the days of ignorance are the best in Islam, provided they gain understanding in the religion."" (The meaning is that if a person is naturally generous and honorable in the days of ignorance, then in Islam he will be even better.)"
"97","It is narrated from Muhammad bin Ali bin Hanafiyyah in the explanation of this verse: «‏ هَلْ جَزَاءُ الإِحْسَانِ إِلاَّ الإِحْسَانُ » ""Is there any reward for good other than good?"" This verse has been written for both the righteous and the wicked. Abu Abdullah, may Allah have mercy on him, said: The statement of Abu Ubaid is: «مسجلة» meaning this verse has been sent (revealed)."
"98","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the one who strives to provide for widows and the poor is like the one who fights in the way of Allah, or like the one who fasts during the day and stands (in prayer) at night."
"99","It is narrated from the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ), Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), that a woman came to me with two girls. She asked me for something, but I could not find anything except one date. So I gave her the date. She divided it into two pieces and gave them to her daughters. After that, she got up and left. Then when the Prophet (ﷺ) came, I told him this story. He said: Whoever is responsible for any of these daughters and treats them well, they will become a shield for him from Hell."
"100","Umm Sa'id bint Murrah Fihri narrates from her father, and he from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I and the one who takes care of an orphan will be in Paradise like this, or like this."" Sufyan was unsure whether he said « كهكَهَاتَيْنِ » or « كَهَذِهِ مِنْ هَذِهِ ‏ .» , and after that, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) joined his middle finger and index finger (to indicate this)."
"101","Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: “I and the sponsor of an orphan will be in Paradise like this,” and he (peace be upon him) gestured with his index finger and middle finger."
"102","Abu Bakr bin Hafs narrates that Abdullah would not eat at his dining mat without having an orphan with him."
"103","It is narrated from Abdur Rahman bin Abzi, he says, Dawood says, ""Be to the orphan like a compassionate father, and also know that as you sow, so shall you reap. How bad it is to become needy after being wealthy, and even worse or more severe than this is that a person goes astray after receiving guidance. When you make a promise to your companion, fulfill whatever promise you make; if you do not do so, enmity will be created between you and him. And seek Allah's refuge from such a companion who does not help you when you remember, and does not remind you when you forget."""
"104","It is narrated from Asma bin Ubaid: I said to Ibn Sirin, ""I have an orphan with me."" He said, ""Treat him as you would treat your own real son, and for disciplining him, strike him with that which you would use to strike your own son."""
"105","Shumaisa ‘Atkiyyah says: The topic of disciplining an orphan was mentioned in the presence of Sayyidah ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), so she said: I beat the orphan so much that he lies down on the ground."
"106","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The Fire of Hell will not touch any Muslim whose three children have died, except to fulfill an oath."" (Which is in this verse: « وَإِنْ مِنْكُمْ إِلَّا وَارِدُهَا كَانَ عَلَى رَبِّكَ حَتْمًا مَقْضِيًّا » )."
"107","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that a woman came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a child and said, ""Pray for him (that he may live); I have already buried three children."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You have built a very strong fence to protect yourself from Hell."""
"108","Khalid Absi says, I had a son who passed away. I was greatly grieved by his loss, so I said to Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him): What have you heard from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) by which we can comfort our hearts over the sorrow of our deceased? He said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Your little children are the «دعاميص» of Paradise."" Explanation of da‘amis: Ibn Kathir says: «دعاميص» is originally the plural of «دعموص» . It is said about an insect that is found in stagnant water. Similarly, « دعموص» is also said for anyone who enters any place, meaning these children will roam freely in Paradise, will enter homes, and will not be forbidden from going anywhere."
"109","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, ""Whoever has three children die and he remains patient, hoping for reward, he will enter Paradise."" We said, ""O Messenger of Allah! And if two children (die)?"" He said, ""And two children as well."" I said to Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him): I think if you people had said one child, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would have said one child as well. Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""By Allah, I think the same."""
"110","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he states that a woman came to the service of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah! We cannot attend your gatherings, so please appoint a separate day for us so that we may come to you on that day. He said: ""Your appointed time is at the house of so-and-so."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to those women and gave them some advice, among which was this: ""Whoever among you has three children die and she remains patient, she will enter Paradise."" A woman asked: And two children? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""And two children as well."" In this narration is Suhail, who was strict in hadith and used to memorize, and no one had the courage to write in his presence."
"111","It is narrated from Sayyida Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: One day I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: ""O Umm Sulaym! If any Muslim (husband and wife) lose three children, Allah will, by His mercy, admit both of them to Paradise."" I asked: (O Messenger of Allah!) And if they lose two children as well? He said: ""And two as well."""
"112","Sayyiduna Sa’sa’ah bin Mu’awiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that he met Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) who was carrying a water-skin hanging from his neck. Sa’sa’ah said: O Abu Dharr! How many children do you have? He replied: I will not tell you. I said: You must tell me. He said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Any Muslim whose three children die before reaching puberty, Allah will admit him to Paradise out of His mercy for them. And whoever frees a Muslim, Allah the Exalted will save each of his limbs from Hell in exchange for each limb of the one he freed."
"113","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever has three children die while they were not yet of age (i.e., had not reached puberty), Allah Almighty will admit that person and those children into Paradise by His mercy."""
"114","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Who among you is there who loves the wealth of his heir more than his own wealth?” The people said: O Messenger of Allah! There is none among us but that he loves his own wealth more than the wealth of his heir. Upon this, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Know that there is none among you but that he loves the wealth of his heir more than his own wealth. Your wealth is only that which you have spent and sent forward, and the wealth of your heir is that which you have accumulated and left behind.”"
"115","Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whom do you count as barren among you?"" The people replied: The barren is the one who has no children. He said: ""No, rather the barren is the one who has not sent anything ahead from his children."" (That is, none of his children died in childhood.)"
"116","Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked, ""Whom do you count as a strong man among you?"" The people replied, ""The one whom no one can overpower."" He (peace be upon him) said, ""No, rather the real strong man is the one who controls himself when he is angry."""
"117","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: “Accept the invitation of the one who invites you, do not return a gift, and do not beat the Muslims.”"
"118","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah's blessings be upon him, that the last words of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, were: ""Take care of the prayer, take care of the prayer, and fear Allah regarding your slaves."""
"119","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Darda’ (may Allah be pleased with him) that he used to say to the people: “We recognize you better than animal doctors recognize animals. We have recognized the good and the bad among you. Your good ones are those from whom good is expected and from whose evil people are safe. And your bad ones are those from whom no good is expected and from whose evil people are not safe, and whose freed slave is not made a slave again.” (That is, after freeing a person, one should not keep making him work by reminding him of the favor.)"
"120","Umrah narrates that Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) made one of her slave girls a mudabbirah (i.e., she said to her, ""You will be free after my death""). After that, Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) fell ill. Her nephews called a physician from a Sudanese (Indian) tribe. He said: ""You are telling me about a woman who has been bewitched by her slave girl."" Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) was informed of this. So she asked the slave girl: ""Did you bewitch me?"" She said: ""Yes."" Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) asked: ""Why did you bewitch me? Now you will never be saved."" Then she said: ""Sell her to some ill-mannered Bedouin."""
"121","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and with him were two slaves. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave one of them to Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah's blessings be upon him) and said: ""Do not beat him, I have been forbidden from beating those who pray, and since we have come, I have seen him performing prayer."" And he gave the other slave to Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: ""Take my advice to treat him well."" Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) set him free. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked: ""What did you do with him?"" Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: You commanded me to treat him well, so I set him free."
"122","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah, he had no servant with him. Abu Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him) took my hand and brought me to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah! This is Anas, a sensible and intelligent boy; he will serve you. Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) states: Then I served the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madinah from his arrival until his passing, in both travel and residence, but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never said to me regarding any task I did, ""Why did you do this?"" nor regarding any task I did not do, ""Why did you not do this?"""
"123","Laqeet bin Sabirah narrates from his father, who said: I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) when he had given a shepherd a kid inside the enclosure. The Prophet (ﷺ) said: « لاَ تَحْسِبَنَّ » and did not say: « لاَ تَحْسَبَنَّ » (i.e., he did not pronounce it with a kasrah). Do not think that we have slaughtered a goat for you. We have a hundred goats and we do not want to have more than a hundred. When the shepherd brings a kid, we slaughter a goat in its place so that the number remains a hundred. Among what the Prophet (ﷺ) said was also: ""Do not beat your wife as you beat your slave-girl, and when you rinse your nose, do so thoroughly except when you are fasting."""
"124","Abu Aliah says that we were instructed to seal anything before handing it over to the servants. Measure and count the item before handing it over so that their habits do not get spoiled and we do not become suspicious."
"125","It is narrated from Salman, he said: I count the meaty bones and give them to my servant so that there is no chance for suspicion. In one narration, the words are «خشية الظن» ."
"126","Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qasit reports that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) sent his slave to the market with gold or silver. The slave sold it in exchange but delayed in taking the exchange. When the slave returned, Abdullah bin Umar beat him very severely. He said: Go and bring back the capital that was mine, and do not bring anything in exchange for it. (That is, do not bring silver in exchange for gold, nor gold in exchange for silver.)"
"127","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) who says: I was beating my slave when I heard a voice from behind me, “O Abu Mas’ud! Know that Allah has more power over you than you have over him.” When I turned around, it was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have freed him for the sake of Allah.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Beware! If you had not done so, the Fire would have engulfed you or the Fire would have touched you.”"
"128","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not say, 'May Allah disfigure his face.'"""
"129","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: Never say this: ""May Allah disfigure your face,"" or the face of the one who resembles your face. Because Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, created Adam (peace be upon him) in His image."
"130","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""When any one of you strikes his servant, he should avoid the face."""
"131","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by an animal that had been branded, and smoke was coming out of its nostrils. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""May Allah curse the person who has done this. None of you should brand the face of an animal nor strike it on its face."""
"132","Hilal bin Yasaf says that we were selling cloth in the house of Suwaid bin Muqarrin. A slave girl came out and said something to a man. That man slapped the slave girl, so Suwaid bin Muqarrin said to him: Did you slap her on the face? I found myself to be one of seven persons (i.e., we were seven men) and we had only one servant. One of us slapped her, so the Prophet (ﷺ) ordered that she be set free."
"133","It is narrated from Abu ‘Umar Zadhan, he states that we were with Sayyiduna Ibn ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with them). He called his slave whom he had beaten. He removed the cloth from his back and said: “Are you in pain?” He replied: “No.” So he freed the slave, then picked up a straw from the ground and said: “I will not receive a reward even equal to the weight of this straw.” I said: “O Abu ‘Abdur-Rahman! Why do you say this?” He said: “I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he used to say or he said: ‘Whoever punishes his slave without guilt or slaps him on the face’—and in another narration: ‘Whoever slaps his slave on the face or imposes a punishment on him for something he did not commit, its expiation is that he should set him free.’”"
"134","It is narrated from Ammar bin Yasir that he said: None of you beats his slave while he is unjust except that retribution will be taken from him on the Day of Resurrection."
"135","Abu Laila narrated that Sayyiduna Salman (may Allah be pleased with him) went out while the fodder of his animal was falling down from the manger. Upon this, he said to his servant: If I did not fear retribution, I would have beaten you."
"136","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he reports from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Surely, rights will be given to their owners, to the extent that the hornless goat will take retribution from the horned goat."""
"137","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever strikes someone unjustly, retribution will be taken from him on the Day of Resurrection."""
"138","It is narrated from ‘Ubadah bin Walid bin ‘Ubadah bin Samit: My father and I set out, seeking knowledge among the Ansar before they passed away. The first person we met was Abu Yasar, a companion of the Prophet (ﷺ), and his slave was with him. Abu Yasar was wearing a striped Yemeni cloak and a Ma’afiri cloak, and his slave was also wearing a striped Yemeni cloak and a Ma’afiri cloak. I said to him: O uncle! If you took your slave’s cloak and gave him your Ma’afiri, or took his Ma’afiri and gave him your cloak, then both of you would have a matching set. He placed his hand on my head and said: O Allah! Bless him. O my nephew! These two eyes of mine have seen, these two ears of mine have heard, and my heart has well remembered—and he pointed to the middle of his chest—that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to say: Feed them from what you eat, and clothe them from what you wear. And if I give him worldly goods, it is easier for me than that he should take my good deeds on the Day of Resurrection."
"139","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to advise good treatment of slaves, and he would say: ""Feed them from what you eat, and clothe them from what you wear. And do not punish the creation of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."""
"140","Ma’rur bin Suwaid says: I saw Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him), he was wearing a cloak and his slave was also wearing a cloak. (In another narration: he had a garment and his slave had a cloak, so we said: If you took this and gave him something else, this would become your cloak.) We asked him the reason for this, so he said: I had abused a man. He complained about me to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: “Did you insult his mother?” I said: Yes. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Indeed, your brothers are your servants. Allah has placed them under your authority. So whoever has his brother under his authority, he should feed him with what he eats himself, and clothe him with what he wears himself, and do not burden them with work that is beyond their capacity. If you do assign them a task that is beyond their capacity, then help them with it.”"
"141","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: Help the worker in his work, because the servant who works for Allah is never unsuccessful."
"142","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The right of a slave is his food and clothing, and that he should not be burdened with work beyond his capacity."""
"143","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Miqdam (may Allah be pleased with him) that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whatever you feed yourself is also charity, whatever you feed your children, your wife, and your servant is also charity."""
"144","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best charity is that which leaves sufficiency behind. And the upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin spending on the person whom you support."""
"145","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered to give charity, so a man said: I have one dinar. He said: ""Spend it on yourself."" He said: I have another dinar. He said: ""Spend it on your wife."" He said: I have another dinar besides that. He said: ""Spend it on your servant, and after that you know best (who is most deserving of your spending)."""
"146","It is narrated from Ibn Jurayj, he says that Abu Zubair informed me that he heard a man asking Jabir about a man's servant: when he spares his master from the hardship of cooking food and from its heat, did the Prophet (peace be upon him) command that he be invited to eat? He said: Yes, and if any of you does not like to eat with the servant, then he should at least give him a morsel in his hand."
"147","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""When a servant brings food to any one of you, he should make him sit with him, and if he does not accept, then he should give him something from the food."""
"148","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Mahdhurah (may Allah be pleased with him) that I was sitting with Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) when Safwan bin Umayyah brought a bowl, which some people were carrying in a cloak. They placed it before Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), so Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) called some poor people and some slaves from among the people around him, and they ate with him. Then, on this occasion, he said: ""May Allah do this to the people,"" or he said: ""May Allah curse the people who turn away from their slaves regarding eating together with them."" Safwan said: ""Beware, by Allah! We do not turn away from them, but we prefer ourselves over them. By Allah! We do not eat so much of the good food that we eat ourselves and also feed them. Rather, we prefer them over ourselves. By Allah! We do not eat good food ourselves and also feed them."""
"149","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If a slave is sincere to his master and worships his Lord well, he will receive a double reward."""
"150","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""There are three types of people who will have a double reward: A man from the People of the Book who believed in his Prophet and also believed in Muhammad (peace be upon him), for him there are two rewards; and a slave who fulfilled the right of Allah and the right of his masters (and in one narration: fulfilled the right of his king who owns him); and a man who had a slave-girl with whom he fulfilled the rights of marriage, taught her discipline and taught her good discipline, and educated her and gave her good education, then set her free and married her, for him there are two rewards."" ‘Amir said: We have given you this hadith for free, that is, without anything in exchange, whereas for a hadith of lesser rank, one would have to travel as far as Madinah."
"151","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware! Each of you is a shepherd, and each of you will be questioned about his flock. The leader who is appointed over the people is a shepherd and will be questioned about his flock. A man is a shepherd over the members of his household and will be questioned about his flock. A man's slave—and in another narration, his servant—is a shepherd over his master's wealth and will be questioned about it. And a woman is a shepherd over her husband's house and will be questioned about it."" I heard all these things from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and I think the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) also said: ""And a man is a shepherd over his father's wealth. Beware! All of you are shepherds, and all of you will be questioned about your flock."""
"152","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When a Muslim slave fulfills the rights of Allah and the rights of his master, he will have a double reward. (Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah said:) By Him in Whose hand is the soul of Abu Hurairah! If striving in the way of Allah, Hajj, and good conduct with my mother did not prevent me, I would have liked that I die in the state that I am a slave."""
"153","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""None of you should say, 'my slave, my slave-girl.' You are all Allah's slaves and all your women are Allah's slave-girls. Rather, you should say: 'my boy, my girl, my young man, my young woman.'"""
"154","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""None of you should say, 'my slave man' or 'my slave woman,' and a slave should not say, 'my lord' or 'my lady.' The master should say, 'my young man' and 'my young woman,' and the slave should say, 'my master' and 'my mistress (my master and my mistress).' All of you are slaves, and the Lord is Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."""
"155","Mutarrif narrates from his father that he said: I went with the delegation of Banu Amir to the service of the Prophet (ﷺ). The people said to the Prophet (ﷺ), ""You are our master."" He replied, ""The Master is Allah."" The people said, ""You are superior to us in excellence, wealth, and spending."" He replied, ""Say whatever you wish, but let not Satan mislead you."""
"156","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sulaiman Malik bin Huwairith (may Allah be pleased with him), he stated that we came to serve the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a state that we were young and of similar age. We stayed with him for twenty days. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) realized that we had become homesick for our families. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked us: ""Which (relatives) have we left behind among our families?"" We informed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was very kind-hearted and compassionate. He said: ""Alright, return to your families. Teach them and instruct them. And perform the prayer as you have seen me performing the prayer. When the time for prayer comes, let one of you give the call to prayer (adhan), and let the eldest among you lead the congregation."""
"157","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah Ansari that he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever is treated kindly should repay it; if he cannot find anything with which to repay it, then he should praise him, for when he praises him, he has expressed gratitude to him. If he conceals his favor, he has shown ingratitude. And whoever describes himself with a quality that is not in him, it is as if he has put on two garments of falsehood."""
"158","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever seeks refuge with Allah, grant him refuge; and whoever asks in the name of Allah, give to him; and whoever does good to you, repay him; and if you cannot find anything with which to repay him, then pray for him until you feel that you have repaid him."""
"159","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Muhajirun said, ""O Messenger of Allah! The Ansar have taken all the reward."" He replied, ""No, as long as you continue to pray for them and praise them, you will also receive the reward."""
"160","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever does not thank people, does not thank Allah either."""
"161","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty said to the soul: 'Come out.' It said: 'I will not come out except unwillingly.'"""
"162","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that it was asked of him, and in another narration, Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) asked the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Which deed is the best among deeds?"" And in another narration: ""Which deed is the most virtuous among deeds?"" He replied: ""To have faith in Allah and to strive in His path."" In another narration, it was asked: ""Which slave is best to set free?"" He replied: ""The one whose price is highest and who is most valuable to his owners."" I asked: ""Tell me, if I am not able to do that?"" He replied: ""Help someone who is helpless (not skilled) or make something for someone who is unskilled."" I asked: ""Tell me, if I become too weak (to do even that)?"" He replied: ""Keep your harm away from people; this too is charity with which you give charity to your own self."""
"163","Sayyiduna Qabeesah bin Barmah Asadi رضي الله عنه reports that I was present in the service of the Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم when I heard him say: ""Those who do good in this world are the ones who will deserve good treatment in the Hereafter, and those who do evil in this world are the ones who will deserve evil treatment in the Hereafter."""
"164","Mu'tamir narrated to us, he says: I narrated to my father the hadith of Abu 'Uthman, who narrates from Salman, that he said: Those who do good in this world are the ones deserving of good treatment in the Hereafter. So he said: I heard this from Abu 'Uthman, and he used to narrate from Salman, so I realized that this is the same, and I have never narrated this hadith to anyone. And in another narration: It is narrated from Abu 'Uthman that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to say the same as Mu'tamir has narrated."
"165","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""Every good deed is charity."""
"166","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Charity is obligatory upon every Muslim.” The people asked: What if someone does not find (anything to give)? He (peace be upon him) said: “He should work with his hands, benefit himself, and give charity.” The people said: What if he is not able to do that or cannot do so? He said: “Then he should help someone in severe need.” The people asked: What if he cannot do even that? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “Then he should enjoin good words,” or he said, “He should enjoin what is good.” The people asked: What if he cannot do even that? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “Then he should refrain from evil; that is charity for him.”"
"167","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: It was said, ""O Messenger of Allah! The wealthy have taken all the reward. They pray as we pray, they fast as we fast, and (in addition to this) they give charity from their surplus wealth."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Has Allah not given you something with which you can give charity? Indeed! Every 'Subhan Allah' and every 'Alhamdulillah' is charity, and for any one of you to fulfill the duty of intimacy with his wife is charity."" It was asked: ""Is there charity even in fulfilling one's desire?"" He replied: ""If he were to fulfill it unlawfully, would he not be sinful? In the same way, if he fulfills it lawfully, there is a reward for him."""
"168","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Barzah Aslami (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! Tell me of an action that will lead me to Paradise."" He said: ""Remove harmful things from the pathways of people."""
"169","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""A Muslim man passed by a thorny branch that was on the road. He said: I will surely remove these thorns (from the path) so that they do not harm any Muslim person. So that person was forgiven."""
"170","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The good and bad deeds of my Ummah were presented before me, and among their good deeds I found: removing something harmful from the road; and among their bad deeds I found: phlegm that was spat in the mosque and not buried."""
"171","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Yazid Khutami (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Every good deed is charity."""
"172","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: Whenever anything was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would say: ""Take this to such-and-such woman, she was a friend of Khadijah. Take this to the house of such-and-such woman, she loved Khadijah."""
"173","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Hudhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: Your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Every good deed is charity."""
"174","Amr bin Abu Qurrah Kindi says: My father proposed the hand of his sister in marriage before Salman (may Allah be pleased with him), but he refused and married his freed slave woman whose name was Baqirah. Abu Qurrah heard that there was some issue (some discord) between Hudhayfah and Salman, so he came looking for Salman. He was told that Salman was at his vegetable beds (in his field). He went in that direction and met Salman, who was carrying a basket on his shoulder filled with vegetables, and his staff was placed in the handle of the basket. Abu Qurrah said: O Abu Abdullah! What is the matter (discord) between you and Hudhayfah? It is narrated: Salman said: «‏ وَكَانَ الإِنْسَانُ عَجُولاً » ""Man is ever hasty."" We (Abu Qurrah and Salman) kept walking until we reached Salman's house. Salman entered his house and said: ""As-salamu 'alaykum,"" then he permitted Abu Qurrah to enter, so he also entered and saw that there was a leather bed placed at the door, with some bricks at its edge and a little saddle cloth. He said: Sit on the bed of his slave woman; this is the bed she lays out for herself (this is an account of the extreme simplicity of the Companions, meaning that a leather mattress was laid out, bricks were placed, and a saddle was placed on the bricks, making it into a pillow). There was a bed, bricks placed at the head, some pieces of vegetables lying around. Salman said: Sit on the bed of his slave woman which she has kept for herself. Then he began to explain to him, saying: The reason for the discord between me and Hudhayfah was that Hudhayfah used to narrate some hadiths, and those were words the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say to people in a state of anger, so people would come to me asking about those matters, whether it was permissible to say them or not. (Hudhayfah used to say that these hadiths were narrated by the Prophet (peace be upon him), so we can also say them, whereas Salman's opinion was that since the Prophet (peace be upon him) said them in anger, we cannot say them.) I would say: Hudhayfah knows best what he says, only he knows, and I disliked that enmity should increase among people. Some people went to Hudhayfah and said: Salman neither affirms you nor denies you in what you say. So Hudhayfah came to me (meaning Hudhayfah demanded that Salman affirm him). He said: O Salman, son of Umm Salman! (i.e., he spoke harsh words, so Salman says that I also became angry) so I said: O Hudhayfah, son of Umm Hudhayfah! You better stop, otherwise I will write to Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) about you. When I threatened him with Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), he left me alone, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am from the children of Adam; if I have unjustly cursed or spoken harshly to any servant, O Allah, make it a mercy for him."" Then they continued talking. He said that Hudhayfah used to narrate those things which the Messenger (peace be upon him) said to some people in a state of anger. These things were brought to me and I was asked about them, so I said that Hudhayfah knows best what he narrates. I disliked that malice should spread among people. People went to Hudhayfah and said that Salman neither affirms you nor denies you. After that, Hudhayfah came to me and said: O Salman, son of Umm Salman! I also said: O Hudhayfah, son of Umm Hudhayfah! Either stop this behavior or I will write to Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). When I threatened him with Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), he left me alone, and the Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If I curse anyone among the children of Adam or speak harshly to him against his will, then I am actually making it a mercy for him."""
"175","Abu Salamah says, I came to Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), he was my friend. I said to him: Will you go with me to the garden? He came out, and he was wearing a black woolen garment. At that time, he was wrapped in a black cloak."
"176","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah send blessings upon him) says, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) to climb a tree and bring a miswak or something similar from it. So his companions saw Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud’s (may Allah be pleased with him) shin, and when they saw his thin shins, they laughed. Upon this, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “What are you laughing at? Abdullah’s leg will be heavier on the scale (on the Day of Resurrection) than Uhud (mountain).”"
"177","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: A believer is a mirror to his brother; when he sees a fault in him, he corrects it."
"178","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""A believer is the mirror of his brother, and a believer is the brother of another believer. He safeguards his belongings, supports him in his absence, and protects him from behind."""
"179","Sayyiduna Mustawrid (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever eats (i.e., obtains) something after speaking ill of a Muslim / whoever makes a Muslim a means of obtaining food. (This means that when a man has a quarrel with someone, another person goes to him and speaks ill of the one with whom he had the quarrel, and by speaking against him, he establishes his own position with the other so that he may be liked as an enemy of his enemy, and in this act of speaking ill, he is given something as a gesture of closeness.) Allah will feed him from the Hellfire in the same way, and whoever is clothed with something in return for speaking ill of a Muslim, Allah will clothe him with something from the Hellfire, and whoever stands at a place of fame and show due to speaking ill of someone (he mentions the faults of another so that he may gain fame and a position), Allah will make him stand at a place of fame and show on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever eats a morsel belonging to a Muslim, Allah will feed him a similar morsel from Hell; and whoever wears a garment belonging to a Muslim, Allah will clothe him with a garment from Hell; and whoever stands in opposition to a Muslim, Allah will stand him in opposition to Himself."""
"180","Abdullah bin Sa’ib narrates from his father, who narrates from his grandfather Yazid bin Sa’id, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), that is, he used to say: “None of you should take anything belonging to his friend, neither in jest nor in seriousness, and if anyone takes his friend’s stick, he should return it to him.”"
"181","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Mas’ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: A man came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, “My mount has become exhausted, please help me to ride (grant me a mount).” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “I do not have one, but go to so-and-so, perhaps he will give you a mount.” He went to him, and he provided him with a mount (he gave him a ride). He returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Whoever guides to a good deed will have a reward equal to that of the one who does it (whoever shows the way to goodness, he will have a reward equal to the one who acts upon it).”"
"182","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): A Jewish woman brought poisoned meat of a goat to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate from that meat. (When the matter became known,) the woman was brought (before him). It was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Should we not kill this Jewish woman? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No."" Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I always used to see the effect of that poison on the throat (uvula) of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"183","Wahb bin Kaysan says, I heard Abdullah bin Zubair saying from the pulpit: ""Adopt the way of forgiveness, enjoin what is good, and turn away from the ignorant."" He said: By Allah! Allah has not commanded this (forgiveness) except that it be taken from people's character. (Meaning, when people behave harshly, one should deal with them with forgiveness.) By Allah! I will certainly take this from the people as long as I live among them (that is, whenever people behave rudely, I will forgive them)."
"184","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Teach and make things easy,"" he said this three times. ""And do not make things difficult, and when any one of you becomes angry, he should remain silent,"" he said this two times."
"185","It is narrated from Ata bin Yasar, he says: I met Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with him), so I said (to him): Tell me the attributes of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that are in the Torah. He said: Yes, by Allah! Some of the attributes of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that are mentioned in the Torah are also described in the Qur'an: « يَا أَيُّهَا النَّبِيُّ إِنَّا أَرْسَلْنَاكَ شَاهِدًا وَمُبَشِّرًا وَنَذِيرًا ‏» ""O Prophet (peace and blessings be upon you)! We have sent you as a witness, a bearer of glad tidings, and a warner."" And as a protector for the unlettered people. You are My servant and My messenger. I have named you 'Al-Mutawakkil' (the one who relies on Allah). You are neither harsh in nature nor hard-hearted, nor do you raise your voice in the markets, nor do you repay evil with evil, but you forgive and overlook. And Allah, the Exalted, will not take him (the Prophet) from this world until, through him, He straightens the crooked nation so that they say 'La ilaha illallah' (there is no god but Allah), and through him, He opens blind eyes, deaf ears, and wrapped hearts."
"186","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I heard a statement from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from which Allah benefited me. I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying, or he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""When you seek out people's faults, you will corrupt them."" I do not seek out their faults lest I corrupt them."
"187","Sayyiduna Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Ever since I became Muslim, whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saw me, he smiled at me."
"188","And the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""From this door, a noble man from Yemen will enter, and an angel has touched his face (meaning he is extremely handsome and beautiful)."" After that, Jarir entered."
"189","It is narrated from the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ), Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) laugh so openly that I could see the uvula of his throat. He (ﷺ) would only smile. Whenever he (ﷺ) saw a dark cloud or a storm, the effects (of terror and fear) would be visible on his (ﷺ) face. And in another narration: When he (ﷺ) saw a cloud with thunder and rain, he would sometimes come inside, sometimes go outside, sometimes come, sometimes go, and his face would change. When it rained, this state of his would go away. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: O Messenger of Allah! When people see a dark cloud, they become happy, hoping that it will rain, but when you see it, signs of displeasure appear on your face. So the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""O Aisha! I am not secure from it, for there may be punishment in it. A people were punished with a wind, and another people saw a similar punishment. People used to say: This is a cloud that will bring us rain."" And in another chain: ""And I do not know, perhaps it is as Allah has said: When they saw it as a cloud advancing towards their valleys, they said: «‏ هَذَا عَارِضٌ مُمْطِرُنَا » ."""
"190","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do less,"" and in another narration: ""Do not laugh too much, for indeed excessive laughter deadens the heart."""
"191","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went to some of his companions who were laughing and talking. Upon this, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Him in Whose hand is my soul, if you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) turned back and made the people weep. And Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, sent revelation to him: O Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), why do you make My servants despair? So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) returned and said: ""Rejoice, follow the straight path, and come closer to one another."""
"192","It is narrated from Musa bin Muslim, from the slave of Qariz’s daughter, that he narrates from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he would often narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), so he would say: This hadith was narrated to me by the one with long eyelashes and white sides. When he turned his attention, he would turn with his whole body, and when he turned his back, he would turn his whole back. No eye has seen anyone like him, nor will it ever see. He whose lips were beautiful, complexion was inclined to whiteness, and when he came forward, he was complete in every way, and when he turned away, he was complete in every way. No eye has ever seen anyone like him, nor will it ever be able to see."
"193","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu’l-Haytham: “Do you have a servant?” He replied, “No.” The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “When captives are brought to us, come as well.” Two captives were brought to the Prophet (peace be upon him), and there was no third with them. At that time, Abu’l-Haytham also came. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said to him: “Choose one of these two.” He replied, “O Messenger of Allah! You choose for me.” The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “The one who is consulted is a trustee. Take this one, for I have seen him performing prayer, and accept my advice to treat him well.” Abu’l-Haytham’s wife said: “You will not be able to keep him as well as the Messenger (peace be upon him) has advised, unless you set him free.” Abu’l-Haytham said: “Then he is free.” Upon this, the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “Allah has not sent any prophet or his successor except that he had two types of confidants: one confidant who commands him to do good and forbids him from evil, and others who do not fall short in trying to harm him. And whoever is protected from the evil confidants has truly been protected.”"
"194","Amr bin Dinar narrates that Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) recited the verse: ""And consult them in some matters."""
"195","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Hasan (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: By Allah, whenever a people adopted the way of consultation, they were guided to the best course. Then he recited this verse, ""And their affairs are (decided) by mutual consultation among them."""
"196","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him). He said that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever attributes a false statement to me which I did not say, let him prepare his abode in Hell. And whoever gives advice to his Muslim brother which, in his view, is not correct, he has committed a betrayal."""
"197","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose hand is my soul, you will not enter Paradise until you become Muslims, and you will not become Muslims until you love one another. Spread the greeting of peace among yourselves, for this will cause you to love one another, and beware of mutual hatred, for indeed it is the shaver. I do not say that it shaves hair, but rather it shaves the religion."""
"198","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that he said: Blessings are shown ingratitude, and ties of kinship are severed, and we have not seen anything like the closeness of hearts."
"199","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to one of his wives, and Umm Sulaym was also with her. And in another chain of narration: Bara’ bin Malik was singing the camel-driving song with the men, and Anjasha was singing the camel-driving song with the women, and Anjasha had a beautiful voice. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “O Anjasha! Drive gently with the glass bottles.” Abu Qilabah said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used such a word that if any of you had said it, you would have found fault with him. His words were: “Driving and leading glass bottles.” (Camel-driving song: a chant sung to make the camels walk faster.)"
"200","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the people said: O Messenger of Allah! Do you joke with us? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed, I do not say anything except the truth."""
"201","It is narrated from Bakr bin Abdullah that he said: The companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) used to throw pieces of watermelon at each other (in jest), but when it came to serious matters, they were true men of the field."
"202","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: A man came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He requested a mount from you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I will mount you on the child of a she-camel."" He said: O Messenger of Allah! What will I do with the child of a she-camel? Upon this, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""And do not camels only give birth to she-camels?"""
"203","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Indeed, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to mingle with us so much that he would say to my younger brother, ""O Abu Umair! What did the little bird do?"""
"204","Sayyiduna Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""There is nothing heavier in the scale than good character."""
"205","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was neither indecent in speech nor did he speak indecently deliberately, and he (peace be upon him) used to say: ""The best among you are those who have the best character."""
"206","Amr bin Shu’aib narrates from his father, and he from his grandfather, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Shall I not tell you who among you is the dearest to me and who will be closest to me on the Day of Resurrection?” All the people remained silent. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) repeated this two or three times. The people said: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “The one among you who has the best character.”"
"207","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been sent only to perfect good character."""
"208","Narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her): She said, whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was given a choice between two matters, he would choose the easier of the two, as long as it was not sinful. But if it was sinful, then he would be the farthest of all people from it. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never took revenge for his own sake, except when one of the sanctities of Allah the Exalted was violated, then he would take revenge for the sake of Allah the Exalted."
"209","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: Verily, Allah Almighty has distributed character among you just as He has distributed sustenance among you. And Allah gives wealth to those whom He loves and (also to) those whom He does not love. He has distributed character among you just as He has distributed your sustenance, and He gives faith only to those whom He loves. Whoever is miserly in spending wealth, fears to fight the enemy, and is afraid to endure the hardship of the night, then he should frequently recite these words: L « اَ إِلَهَ إِلاَّ اللَّهُ ، وَسُبْحَانَ اللهِ ، وَالْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ ، وَاللَّهُ أَكْبَرُ » ."
"210","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""Wealth is not due to having a lot of possessions, but true wealth is the richness of the heart."""
"211","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I served the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for ten years, but he never even said ""uff"" to me, and regarding something I did not do, he never said, ""Why did you not do it?"" And regarding something I did do, he never said, ""Why did you do this?"""
"212","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was very compassionate. When anyone came to him (for their need), he would make a promise to them and fulfill it, provided he had it with him. (Once) the iqamah for prayer was given and a Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), grabbed his garment, and said: ""I have a small need left, I fear I might forget it."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went with him until his need was fulfilled, and then returned and led the prayer."
"213","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never said ""no"" in response to any request."
"214","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I have not seen any two women more generous than Sayyidah Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) and Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her). The manner of their generosity was different. Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) used to accumulate wealth, and when some wealth was collected with her, she would distribute it. As for Asma (may Allah be pleased with her), her way was that she would not save anything for the next day (i.e., she would spend whatever she had each day)."
"215","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The dust encountered in the way of Allah and the smoke of Hell will never be combined in the belly of a servant. And (likewise) miserliness and faith can never be gathered together in the heart of a servant."""
"216","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Rabee’ah, he says: We were sitting with Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ood (may Allah be pleased with him), and he mentioned a man and described his character and habits. Abdullah said: Tell me, if you cut off this person’s head, can you then reattach it? The people said: No. He said: Well, if you cut off his hand? The people said: No. He said: And his stomach? The people said: No. He said: Then you cannot change his habits either until you change his physical structure. Indeed, the drop (of semen) remains in the womb for forty days, then it becomes blood and descends, then it becomes a clot, then it becomes a lump of flesh, then Allah sends an angel who writes down his provision, his character, and whether he will be fortunate or unfortunate."
"217","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed, a person, due to good character, attains the rank of one who stands (in prayer) at night."""
"218","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard Abul-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""The best among you in Islam are those who are best in character, provided they have understanding of the religion."""
"219","Thabit bin Ubaid says that I have not seen anyone more dignified in gatherings and more cheerful at home than Sayyiduna Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"220","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked: ""Which religion does Allah Almighty like the most?"" He replied: ""The upright religion which is the easy way."""
"221","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) says: There are four qualities; if you attain them, then whatever else of the world passes you by, you will not be harmed: good character, pure and lawful food, truthful speech, and safeguarding trust."
"222","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you know which thing leads most to Hell?"" The people said, ""Allah and His Messenger (peace be upon him) know best."" He said: ""The two hollow things: the private parts and the mouth. And which thing leads most to Paradise? Fear of Allah and good character."""
"223","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Usama bin Sharik (may Allah be pleased with him) who says: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when many Bedouins came to him from here and there. So everyone became silent, only those people began to speak. They submitted: O Messenger of Allah! Is there any harm in doing this, is there any harm in doing that? They asked about some matters among people's affairs in which there was no harm. Upon this, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O servants of Allah! Allah has removed all harm except for the person who cuts off his brother unjustly, that is, he backbites him. This is the person who has fallen into hardship and has been destroyed."" They asked: O Messenger! Can we seek treatment? He said: ""Yes, O servants of Allah! Seek treatment, for Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has not sent down any disease except that He has also sent down its cure, except for one disease."" They asked: O Messenger of Allah! And what is that? He said: ""Old age."" The people submitted: O Messenger of Allah! What is the best thing given to a person? He said: ""Good character."""
"224","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was the most generous of all people in goodness, and he was most generous during Ramadan when Jibril (peace be upon him) would meet him. Jibril would meet him every night of Ramadan, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would present the Qur'an to him. And when Jibril met him, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was more generous in goodness than the sent wind."
"225","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Mas’ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The account of a man from among the people before you was taken, and no good deed was found for him except that he used to mix with people and was wealthy, so he would order his servants to show leniency to those in difficulty. So Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said: We are more deserving of doing that than he was, so Allah forgave him.”"
"226","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Nawwas bin Sam'an Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about virtue and sin. So he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Virtue is good character, and sin is that which pricks your heart and you dislike that people become aware of it."""
"227","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Banu Salamah, who is your chief?"" We replied: Jad bin Qais, although we consider him to be miserly. He said: ""What disease can be more destructive than miserliness? Rather, your chief is 'Amr bin Jamuh."" In the days of ignorance, 'Amr used to look after their idols, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would marry, he ('Amr) would arrange the wedding feast on his behalf."
"228","Warrad, the scribe of Sayyiduna Mughirah (may Allah be pleased with him), narrates that Sayyiduna Muawiyah (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote a letter to Sayyiduna Mughirah bin Shu’bah (may Allah be pleased with him): ""Send me something in writing that you have heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)."" So Sayyiduna Mughirah (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote to him. (And in one narration, Warrad said: He dictated to me and I wrote it with my own hand.) Indeed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) (and in another narration: I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him) «قيل و قال» (idle talk), wasting wealth, asking too many questions, withholding (people’s rights), and making unlawful demands (i.e., asking for what one is not entitled to, making illegitimate demands), disobedience to mothers, and burying daughters alive."
"229","Sayyiduna Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a message to me and ordered me to come to him fully dressed and armed. So I complied, and when I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he was performing ablution. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his gaze towards me and then lowered it. After that, he said: ""O Amr! I intend to appoint you as the commander of an army, so Allah will grant you spoils of war, and I desire for you what is lawful from your wealth."" I said: O Messenger of Allah! I did not accept Islam for the sake of wealth. I became Muslim seeking Islam so that I could be with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."" He said: ""O Amr! Lawful provision is very good for a righteous man."""
"230","Sayyiduna Ubaydullah bin Mihsan Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever wakes up in the morning while his soul is at peace, his body is healthy, and he has food for one day, then it is as if the whole world has been gathered for him."""
"231","Abdullah bin Khubaib Juhani narrates from his uncle that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to him and there were signs of bathing upon him, and he was very happy. We thought that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had gone to his family. So we said: O Messenger of Allah! We see you in a very happy mood? Then when wealth was mentioned, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""For a person who is pious, having wealth is not a sin, and for a person who is pious, good health is better than wealth, and being cheerful is also among the blessings of Allah."""
"232","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was the most handsome of all people, the most generous of all, and the bravest of all. One night, the people of Madinah were frightened, so they headed towards the direction from which the noise had come. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was coming back from that direction ahead of them—he had reached the source of the sound before anyone else. He (peace and blessings be upon him) was saying: “Do not be afraid, do not be afraid.” At that time, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was riding the horse of Abu Talhah without a saddle, on its bare back. A sword was hanging from his neck. He said: “I found it (the horse) to be like the sea,” or he said, “Indeed, it is like the sea (i.e., very swift).”"
"233","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), he said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every good deed is charity, and among the good deeds is that you meet your brother with a cheerful face, and that you pour (water) from your bucket into your brother's vessel."""
"234","Narrated from Yazid bin Babnoos: We went to Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) and asked: O Mother of the Believers! What was the character of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)? Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: His character was the Qur'an."
"235","It is narrated from Salim bin Abdullah, he said: I never heard Abdullah (ibn Umar) (may Allah be pleased with them) curse any person, nor anything else. Salim says that Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not befitting for a believer to be one who curses."""
"236","It is narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Jews came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said «السام عليكم» (may destruction be upon you). Upon this, Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: And may destruction be upon you too, and may Allah curse you, and may Allah’s wrath be upon you. Upon this, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Stop, Aisha! You should adopt gentleness, and avoid harshness and foul speech.” Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Did you not hear what they said? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “And did you not hear what I said? I returned it upon them. My words will be accepted against them, and their curse will not be accepted against me.”"
"237","Sayyiduna Abdullah (ibn Mas'ud) (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""A believer is neither one who taunts, nor one who curses, nor one who uses obscene language, nor one who abuses."""
"238","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""A two-faced person is not worthy of being trustworthy."""
"239","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah (ibn Mas'ud) رضي الله عنه that he said: Among the morals of a believer, the most blameworthy is idle talk."
"240","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Those who curse will neither be witnesses nor intercessors on the Day of Resurrection."""
"241","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is not befitting for a truthful person to be one who curses."""
"242","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Hudhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: Whenever any people invoke a curse, the curse falls upon them."
"243","It is narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) cursed one of his slaves, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Abu Bakr! One who curses and also the Siddiq? Never!"" By the Lord of the Ka'bah! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this two or three times. Upon this, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) freed one of his slaves that day, and afterwards, he presented himself before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I will not do this again."
"244","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said that it was said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah! Pray against the polytheists. He replied: ""I was not sent as one who curses, rather I was sent as a mercy."""
"245","It is narrated from Hammam that we were with Hudhaifah, and it was said to Hudhaifah that a man conveys people's words to Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him). So Hudhaifah said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The tale-bearer will not enter Paradise."""
"246","It is narrated from Sayyidah Asma bint Yazid (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Shall I not tell you who are the best among you?” The people said: Yes. He said: “Those people who, when they are seen, Allah is remembered.” He said: “Shall I not tell you who are the worst among you?” The people said: Yes. He said: “Those who spread gossip, those who create discord among friends, and those who seek out faults in innocent people (seekers of sins).”"
"247","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The one who utters obscene words and the one who spreads them, both have equal sin."
"248","It is narrated from Shabeel bin Auf that he said: It is said that whoever hears an obscene thing and spreads it, then in this matter he is just like the one who initiated it himself."
"249","It is narrated from Ata that he believed that a person who spreads or publicizes acts of adultery, that is, acts of indecency, should be punished."
